# Optional overrides — unifi-network-mcp has no required env vars.
# Authentication is per-request via headers (provided by the MCP caller):
#
#   X-Unifi-Api-Key      A Site Manager API key, generated at
#                        unifi.ui.com > Settings > API Keys — NOT a local
#                        console key (local keys have no meaning to
#                        api.ui.com and will 401).
#
#   X-Unifi-Console-Id   The target console's Site Manager host ID. Find
#                        it via the unifi_list_hosts tool.
#
# Every call goes through Ubiquiti's own cloud
# (https://api.ui.com/v1/connector/consoles/{console_id}/...), which
# proxies to the console — this server never talks to a customer's network
# directly. This is also the only way to reach Official UniFi Hosting
# (Ubiquiti's own SaaS offering), which has no customer-reachable address
# to give as a direct host in the first place. (Direct-to-console mode was
# dropped — see README.)
#
# This server has no shared/brokerable auth layer to delegate to a
# gateway — the customer's own Site Manager API key *is* the credential,
# forwarded as-is on every request, and never persisted beyond one request.

MCP_HTTP_PORT=8080
MCP_HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0
